  {
   "id": "r1n",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1412,
   "width": 934,
   "height": 105,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100139,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700973,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Prices change daily, so rate cannot be a column on room_type - that would store one price for all time. But it is also a\nSEPARATE TABLE FROM INVENTORY rather than another column on the inventory row, for an ownership reason as much as a technical\none: rates are set by revenue management on their own cadence and tooling, while inventory is mutated by the booking path\nthousands of times more often. Putting the rate on the inventory row would mean every price change writes to THE ROW THAT\nBOOKINGS CONTEND ON - adding write contention to the hottest row in the system, for data the booking transaction only reads.\nrate_minor is an integer of minor units: a total assembled from 14 nightly rates would accumulate float representation error\ninto a figure somebody gets charged.",
   "originalText": "Prices change daily, so rate cannot be a column on room_type - that would store one price for all time. But it is also a\nSEPARATE TABLE FROM INVENTORY rather than another column on the inventory row, for an ownership reason as much as a technical\none: rates are set by revenue management on their own cadence and tooling, while inventory is mutated by the booking path\nthousands of times more often. Putting the rate on the inventory row would mean every price change writes to THE ROW THAT\nBOOKINGS CONTEND ON - adding write contention to the hottest row in the system, for data the booking transaction only reads.\nrate_minor is an integer of minor units: a total assembled from 14 nightly rates would accumulate float representation error\ninto a figure somebody gets charged.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "r2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1544,
   "width": 333,
   "height": 17,
   "strokeColor": "#b91c1c",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100140,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700980,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "expires_at exists to drive the sweeper",
   "originalText": "expires_at exists to drive the sweeper",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "r2n",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1570,
   "width": 934,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100141,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700987,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Set when a reservation is created as pending, cleared on confirmation. The mechanism matters: PENDING RESERVATIONS HOLD\nINVENTORY. A checkout abandoned at the payment step has already incremented total_reserved, so without a sweeper that\ninventory is held forever, and the failure mode is availability slowly leaking away - a hotel that looks full and isn't, with\nnothing in the logs to explain it. So the alert is not on the sweeper's completion; it is on INVENTORY CURRENTLY HELD BY\nPENDING ROWS. That is the number that says whether the mechanism is working.",
   "originalText": "Set when a reservation is created as pending, cleared on confirmation. The mechanism matters: PENDING RESERVATIONS HOLD\nINVENTORY. A checkout abandoned at the payment step has already incremented total_reserved, so without a sweeper that\ninventory is held forever, and the failure mode is availability slowly leaking away - a hotel that looks full and isn't, with\nnothing in the logs to explain it. So the alert is not on the sweeper's completion; it is on INVENTORY CURRENTLY HELD BY\nPENDING ROWS. That is the number that says whether the mechanism is working.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d5",
   "type": "line",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1682,
   "width": 1680,
   "height": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#cbd5e1",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
