  {
   "id": "el",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1700,
   "width": 509,
   "height": 21,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100143,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 701001,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Indexes - and one partial index worth the detail",
   "originalText": "Indexes - and one partial index worth the detail",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1738,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 243,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100144,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 701008,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "PRIMARY KEY (hotel_id, room_type_id, date) on room_type_inventory   the availability range scan AND the booking UPDATE, both\n                                                                   as one descent plus a short scan. The most important index\n                                                                   in the design.\nPRIMARY KEY (reservation_id) on reservation                        lookup by id - and the uniqueness that IS idempotency\nINDEX (guest_id, created_at DESC) on reservation                   'my bookings, newest first'. DESC means no sort.\nINDEX (hotel_id, start_date) on reservation                        the front desk's arrivals list, and check-in assignment\nINDEX (status, expires_at) WHERE status = 'pending'                THE SWEEPER'S SCAN, and partial on purpose: the\n                                                                   overwhelming majority of rows are terminal and are not\n                                                                   indexed at all. A full index would grow with total booking\n                                                                   volume to serve a query that only ever wants the handful\n                                                                   in flight.\nPRIMARY KEY (hotel_id, room_type_id, date) on room_type_rate       co-ordered with inventory, so a stay's rates are also one\n                                                                   contiguous scan\nspatial index on (latitude, longitude) on hotel                    search by location - a single-column index on lat OR lng\n                                                                   does not help",
   "originalText": "PRIMARY KEY (hotel_id, room_type_id, date) on room_type_inventory   the availability range scan AND the booking UPDATE, both\n                                                                   as one descent plus a short scan. The most important index\n                                                                   in the design.\nPRIMARY KEY (reservation_id) on reservation                        lookup by id - and the uniqueness that IS idempotency\nINDEX (guest_id, created_at DESC) on reservation                   'my bookings, newest first'. DESC means no sort.\nINDEX (hotel_id, start_date) on reservation                        the front desk's arrivals list, and check-in assignment\nINDEX (status, expires_at) WHERE status = 'pending'                THE SWEEPER'S SCAN, and partial on purpose: the\n                                                                   overwhelming majority of rows are terminal and are not\n                                                                   indexed at all. A full index would grow with total booking\n                                                                   volume to serve a query that only ever wants the handful\n                                                                   in flight.\nPRIMARY KEY (hotel_id, room_type_id, date) on room_type_rate       co-ordered with inventory, so a stay's rates are also one\n                                                                   contiguous scan\nspatial index on (latitude, longitude) on hotel                    search by location - a single-column index on lat OR lng\n                                                                   does not help",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1990,
   "width": 971,
   "height": 48,
   "strokeColor": "#b45309",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100145,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 701015,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Deliberately absent: nothing on total_reserved or total_inventory - they are read as part of the row, never searched by.\nNothing on reservation.status alone (cardinality 4, so the planner would ignore it). And no index on room.room_type_id,\nbecause room assignment is per-hotel and a hotel has tens of rooms, not millions.",
   "originalText": "Deliberately absent: nothing on total_reserved or total_inventory - they are read as part of the row, never searched by.\nNothing on reservation.status alone (cardinality 4, so the planner would ignore it). And no index on room.room_type_id,\nbecause room assignment is per-hotel and a hotel has tens of rooms, not millions.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d6",
   "type": "line",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2050,
   "width": 1680,
   "height": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#cbd5e1",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
