  {
   "id": "fl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2068,
   "width": 1089,
   "height": 21,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100147,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 701029,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The same data has different consistency requirements depending on whether it is DISPLAYED or DECIDED ON",
   "originalText": "The same data has different consistency requirements depending on whether it is DISPLAYED or DECIDED ON",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "fn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2106,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 260,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100148,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 701036,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "room_type_inventory, the write   STRONG, serializable in effect   where double-booking is prevented: the atomic conditional\n                                                                 UPDATE plus the CHECK backstop. Non-negotiable.\nroom_type_inventory, the read    EVENTUAL, from a replica        availability SHOWN to a browsing user may be stale, because\n                                                                 the authoritative check happens again in the transaction\nreservation                      STRONG, read-your-writes       a guest who just booked must see it - and a stale read on\n                                                                 reservation_id would defeat idempotency, creating a second\n                                                                 booking. Primary reads only.\nstatus transitions               STRONG                          a lost pending -> confirmed leaves a PAID reservation\n                                                                 unconfirmed while the sweeper releases its inventory\nhotel / room_type / room         EVENTUAL, long TTL              near-static; a description a few minutes stale is invisible.\n                                                                 The highest-volume read path, and it caches almost perfectly.\nroom_type_rate                   STRONG at booking, eventual for display   a price shown while browsing may be stale; the\n                                                                 price CHARGED must be the one read inside the transaction,\n                                                                 or you charge a rate the user never saw\nthe inventory cache (at scale)   EVENTUAL, CDC-fed               the database remains the authority, so staleness can only\n                                                                 cause a misleading display, never an oversell",
   "originalText": "room_type_inventory, the write   STRONG, serializable in effect   where double-booking is prevented: the atomic conditional\n                                                                 UPDATE plus the CHECK backstop. Non-negotiable.\nroom_type_inventory, the read    EVENTUAL, from a replica        availability SHOWN to a browsing user may be stale, because\n                                                                 the authoritative check happens again in the transaction\nreservation                      STRONG, read-your-writes       a guest who just booked must see it - and a stale read on\n                                                                 reservation_id would defeat idempotency, creating a second\n                                                                 booking. Primary reads only.\nstatus transitions               STRONG                          a lost pending -> confirmed leaves a PAID reservation\n                                                                 unconfirmed while the sweeper releases its inventory\nhotel / room_type / room         EVENTUAL, long TTL              near-static; a description a few minutes stale is invisible.\n                                                                 The highest-volume read path, and it caches almost perfectly.\nroom_type_rate                   STRONG at booking, eventual for display   a price shown while browsing may be stale; the\n                                                                 price CHARGED must be the one read inside the transaction,\n                                                                 or you charge a rate the user never saw\nthe inventory cache (at scale)   EVENTUAL, CDC-fed               the database remains the authority, so staleness can only\n                                                                 cause a misleading display, never an oversell",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "fn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2388,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 32,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100149,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 701043,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Availability, rates and inventory each appear TWICE in that list with different models. Getting that distinction right is what\nlets a system with a hard correctness requirement still serve 1,000x more reads than writes from replicas and caches.",
   "originalText": "Availability, rates and inventory each appear TWICE in that list with different models. Getting that distinction right is what\nlets a system with a hard correctness requirement still serve 1,000x more reads than writes from replicas and caches.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d7",
   "type": "line",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2452,
   "width": 1680,
   "height": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#cbd5e1",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100150,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 701050,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "points": [
    [
     0,
     0
    ],
    [
     1680,
     0
    ]
   ],
   "roundness": null
  },
  {
   "id": "gl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2470,
   "width": 994,
   "height": 21,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100151,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 701057,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "If it had to scale: shard on hotel_id - an unusually clean story, and a property of the DOMAIN",
   "originalText": "If it had to scale: shard on hotel_id - an unusually clean story, and a property of the DOMAIN",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "sh",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2508,
   "width": 760,
   "height": 44,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "#a7f3d0",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100152,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 701064,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "sh_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "sh_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 2521,
   "width": 744,
   "height": 17,
   "strokeColor": "#374151",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100153,
