  {
   "id": "gn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2708,
   "width": 1003,
   "height": 81,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100164,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 701148,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "And the inventory cache, if added, is DISPLAY-ONLY: key {hotel_id}_{room_type_id}_{date} -> available_count, fed by CDC from\nthe replication log. A stale cache can make a user see '1 room left' and then receive a 409 - mildly annoying, and IDENTICAL\nto what already happens when somebody hesitates while browsing and somebody else books first. It cannot cause an oversell,\nbecause the atomic UPDATE and the CHECK constraint are still the gate. That is why cache/database inconsistency is tolerable\nhere when it would be unacceptable in the digital wallet: THE CACHE NEVER PARTICIPATES IN THE DECISION.",
   "originalText": "And the inventory cache, if added, is DISPLAY-ONLY: key {hotel_id}_{room_type_id}_{date} -> available_count, fed by CDC from\nthe replication log. A stale cache can make a user see '1 room left' and then receive a 409 - mildly annoying, and IDENTICAL\nto what already happens when somebody hesitates while browsing and somebody else books first. It cannot cause an oversell,\nbecause the atomic UPDATE and the CHECK constraint are still the gate. That is why cache/database inconsistency is tolerable\nhere when it would be unacceptable in the digital wallet: THE CACHE NEVER PARTICIPATES IN THE DECISION.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  }
